/tmp/claude-1007/-home-yixunhu-codespace-FLAC/1630c6fe-5d3e-42b4-94ec-1b6d3bcb0e4e/scratchpad/r3a/fresh_clone_merged/worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_11_fa_orbit_claude/commits_fa_orbit.md:50:| 41 | `b23fccd` | GO-check NO-GO closure. **ASSETS (the crasher):** `fa_orbit_measure_worktree.sh` links `AcousticRooms` and `weights` into every pinned worktree at the main tree's own targets — a fresh worktree holds only TRACKED files, so the eval's relative `AcousticRooms` / `weights/AGREE/AGREE_fullAR.pt` did not exist and a pinned screen would have died at startup; the screen now stats each required asset before spending a slot. **LIFECYCLE:** fixed-count pruning (which could delete a QUEUED job's tree) is replaced by LEASES — `.leases/<jobid>` written under an `flock` before `sbatch` returns and promoted to the real id, validated by the job at start, released by a trap at exit; a tree is prunable only with zero live leases (stale ids double-checked against `squeue`) and never the tree being handed out. New `fa_orbit_screen_submit.sh` makes pin+lease+submit atomic. **IMMUTABLE LAUNCH BINDING:** the launch manifest lives under gitignored outputs and is mutable, so it is now bound to a committed `arm_launch_registry.json` by sha256 plus job, mode INITIAL, launch uuid, commit, rung, max_steps, config/VAE/P0 hashes, save-dir and seed 42 — the seed used to be printed, not checked. **TABLE:** the two-K gate is transactional (aborts without writing; `--allow-partial-exp11` still renders WITHHELD, never numbers), `build_header()` is actually called by `main()` so the LABEL-MIGRATION-DEFERRED note reaches the file, and `--repo-root` resolves evidence/validator/output against the MAIN tree from any cwd. Also: MEASURE_ROOT must be a detached, managed worktree of THIS repo under `.measure_worktrees/`, and the sidecar records a repo-relative model-config path. |
/tmp/claude-1007/-home-yixunhu-codespace-FLAC/1630c6fe-5d3e-42b4-94ec-1b6d3bcb0e4e/scratchpad/r3a/fresh_clone_merged/worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_11_fa_orbit_claude/commits_fa_orbit.md:51:| 42 | `e650d6a` | GO re-check 2. **LIFECYCLE (the not-closed one):** every store operation — create, lease, release, prune — now takes ONE store-wide `flock` (`.store.lock`), so a sweep can never enumerate leases while a submission writes one; the pin→lease and sbatch→promote races are gone entirely because submission is `sbatch --hold` → job id known → lease written → `scontrol release`, with the held job CANCELLED if either step fails (no orphan, no placeholder); and a nonzero `squeue` is no longer read as job-absent — only Slurm's explicit `Invalid job id` proves absence, everything else (controller down, timeout) keeps the lease and logs. Found while testing: `git worktree remove` leaves the directory behind when our symlinks/leases defeat its cleanup, and because that leftover sits inside the main checkout `git -C` on it answers for the MAIN repo — a stale directory looked like a reusable pinned tree. Identity is now verified (`.git` present, top-level == itself, same common dir) and half-removed entries are cleared. **ASSETS identity:** `AGREE_fullAR.pt` pinned by sha256 `3a13243d…` and gated in the screen exactly as the VAE is in the launcher; the `AcousticRooms` target is pinned literally in the helper, so a repointed main-tree symlink aborts instead of silently swapping the corpus. **CLI:** `main()` parsed `[]` instead of `sys.argv`, so `--repo-root` was accepted and then discarded — every command-line run used the default root; fixed, with a subprocess test from a foreign cwd against real synthetic evidence (it also exposed that the validator's repo root must be importable, else the gate fails closed for the wrong reason). **Validator:** the sidecar's repo-relative `model_config` was opened against the ambient cwd and reported 'not readable' from any pinned worktree; it now resolves against `REPO`/`OUTPUT_ROOT_BASE`, tested from a foreign cwd with the wrong-hash case still rejected. |
